@startuml US4-Reserve-Portions
title US4 - Reserve portions

actor Student
participant "Browser" as Browser
participant "Flask route\nreserve_listing" as Route
participant "ReserveForm" as Form
participant "Listing (Model)" as Listing
participant "Reservation (Model)" as Reservation
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

Student -> Browser: Click "Reserve" on /listings
Browser -> Route: GET /listings/<id>/reserve
note right of Route: role_required(STUDENT) - a vendor or anonymous user never gets here
Route -> DB: SELECT listing WHERE id, not cancelled,\npickup_end > now FOR UPDATE
alt listing missing, cancelled or ended
  Route --> Browser: 404 Not Found
else listing available
  Route --> Browser: Render listings/reserve.html with ReserveForm (1 or 2 portions)
end

Student -> Browser: Choose 1 or 2 portions, click "Reserve"
Browser -> Route: POST /listings/<id>/reserve (with CSRF token)
Route -> DB: SELECT listing ... FOR UPDATE
note right of DB
  the row lock makes a second student's request wait
  until this one commits, so it sees the new
  portions_remaining and cannot overbook (US4.4)
end note
Route -> Form: validate_on_submit()
alt no choice, or a value other than 1 or 2
  Form --> Route: errors
  Route --> Browser: Re-render the form with the error
else valid choice
  Route -> DB: SELECT ACTIVE reservation for (student, listing)
  alt student already has an active reservation
    Route --> Browser: Re-render the form, flash "You already have a reservation for this listing."
  else portions > portions_remaining
    Route --> Browser: Re-render the form, flash "Not enough portions available." (US4.3)
  else enough portions
    Route -> Reservation: generate_pickup_code()
    Reservation -> DB: SELECT reservation by code (repeat until unused)
    Route -> Reservation: new Reservation(student, listing, portions, code, status ACTIVE)
    Route -> Listing: portions_remaining -= portions (US4.2)
    Route -> DB: INSERT reservation, UPDATE listing, COMMIT (releases the lock)
    Route --> Browser: Redirect to /reservations,\nflash "Reserved! Your pickup code is XXXXXX" (US4.1)
  end
end

@enduml
